Package: libva-v4l2-stateful
Architecture: arm64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends},
         qcom-va-driver (>= 1.1.1+gitee8622c-0diting6)
Description: VA-API driver for V4L2 stateful video decoders (Diting iris), kept for snap Chromium
 VA-API backend on top of V4L2 stateful (memory-to-memory) decoders,
 patched for the Qualcomm iris decoder of the Xiaomi 12T Pro (diting):
 H.264, HEVC and VP9 hardware decoding for VA-API applications.
 .
 No longer the default driver. Since 2026-11-28 qcom-va-driver, which this
 package depends on, is installed as msm_drv_video.so, the name libva
 derives from the msm DRM driver, and decodes and encodes for every program
 that does not say otherwise; Firefox, which uses the host's driver, gets a
 default pref here that makes it try hardware decoding on this GPU.
 .
 This driver is installed as v4l2_drv_video.so only, for snap Chromium: the
 snap cannot read host libraries, so a systemd user service copies the file
 into ~/snap/chromium/common/dri at login and points the snap there through
 ~/.chromium-browser.init (see diting-chromium-vaapi).
 .
 A udev rule names the decoder /dev/video-dec0, one of the two paths the
 driver opens (the other, /dev/video0, is the decoder only when it registers
 before the cameras).
